The 42 `jal runtime_error` reachability residuals of `errFamilyClosed`
collapse to **19 distinct `jal` PCs** (the same 19 `errSite_<pc>` classes
`ErrSitesBatch0-3` proved).  Each premise's hsite is `∀ c, JalErrPre S.g
S.inp S.m0 <pc> <bytes> c`, a type fixed by the PC ALONE — so the 23
duplicate PCs let an M6 supplier discharge 19 links, not 42.

`ErrSiteLinks S` bundles the 19; `errFamilyClosed_ofClasses` feeds each of
the 42 route slots the shared per-PC field (a pure projection — the
per-class lemma is the identity).  `JalErrPre` pins `c`'s PC to the error
jal, so NO field is provable unconditionally: the 19 fields ARE the honest
coalesced caller-linkage residual (M4 arm-context → parked-at-jal), i.e. the
`hsite` supplier's remaining work, reduced 42 → 19.

GENERATED by `scripts/gen_m5_error_routing.py` (`emit_classes`).  DO NOT
hand-edit.  NO sorry/axiom/native_decide/bv_decide; no Mathlib.
-/

